When a screenshot covers a subtree whose descendants run in other
WebContent processes, Ladybird has each of those processes paint them
and hand their frames to the compositor before taking the screenshot.
The other engines’ test harnesses do the same before a snapshot:
Blink’s WebTestControlHost::CompositeAllFramesThen() walks the frame
tree and has every local root composite, with SynchronouslyComposite-
AfterTest(), before its CopyFromSurface. WebKit’s WebPageProxy::
updateRenderingWithForcedRepaint() sends UpdateRenderingWithForced-
Repaint to every web content process the page spans, then waits on a
CallbackAggregator for their replies, and for the next presentation
update. And Gecko’s reftest harness sends FlushRendering to every
out-of-process browsing context, through ReftestFissionParent::
tellChildrenToFlushRenderingRecursive(), before its snapshot. Ladybird
does it in the engine’s screenshot path rather than in a harness, so
WebDriver screenshots get the same treatment.
